{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Go forth from the ark, you and your wife, etc.</b> He intended to permit to him something He had forbidden to him at the time of his entry into the ark, and also regarding the other species of creatures HaShem commanded them, and they swarmed and multiplied. And He was precise to say <b>go forth</b>, etc., and afterward mentioned the pairing of males and females, to say that as long as they were in the ark — even though the days of the affliction had been completed — they were under the prohibition of mating until after emerging. And so you will find that the verse says after this: ״וַיֵּצֵא נֹחַ וּבָנָיו וְאִשְׁתּוֹ״ — etc., males alone and females alone, until the time of emergence; for he scrutinized the word of HaShem just as we have scrutinized. Also from what is found therein you know that they kept the commandment of HaShem and were separated from their wives according to the word of the King all the while they were in the ark until they went out, and it is His saying <b>וַיֵּצֵא נֹחַ וּבָנָיו</b> — this points clearly that until the time of emergence they were separated. And see what we have written on the verse (Genesis 9:7) ״וְאַתֶּם פְּרוּ וּרְבוּ״."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:40:15.734070799Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}